'''Timm Karlo''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who worked at [[Caleen Salyard]] on [[Ferrix]] with his eventual lover [[Bix Caleen]].<ref name="Episode 1" /> Jealous<ref name="217 Companion">{{InsiderCite|217|Star Wars: Andor Season One Companion|''Star Wars: Andor'' Season One Companion}}</ref> and drinking, Karlo reported the wanted [[Cassian Jeron Andor]], the ex-boyfriend of Caleen, to [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Preox-Morlana]]. Having seen them talking together,<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref> Karlo was upset but also thought he was protecting Caleen.<ref name="217 Companion" /> He was shot and [[Death|killed]] by Preox-Morlana [[officer]]s after attempting to help Caleen, who had been detained by them after trying to get closer.<ref name="Episode 3" /> By the time Andor returned to Ferrix after the [[Aldhani heist]], it was common knowledge that he was the one who had reported Andor.<ref name="Announcement" />

==Biography==
===Drunken jealousy===
During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[Proclamation of the New Order|successor]] state of the [[Galactic Republic]], the [[Gender|male]] [[human]] Timm Karlo resided on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]], where he worked at [[Caleen Salyard]] with his lover [[Bix Caleen]]. In [[5 BBY]], [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], a former lover of Caleen, arrived at the [[salvage yard]] bruised and beaten. Unbeknownst to Karlo, Andor had returned from the the planet [[Morlana One]] the previous [[Standard day|night]], where he had killed two [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Preox-Morlana]] [[Sentry Corporal|Sentry Corporals]]—[[Verlo Skiff]] and [[Kravas Drezzer]]. Additionally, Andor was in possession of an [[Imperial N-S9 Starpath Unit]], which he planned to sell by way of Caleen's [[black market]] connections.<ref>{{Andor|Kassa}}</ref>

Increasingly suspicious of his intentions, Karlo confronted Andor, believing him to have upset Caleen. Soon after, Bix began to embark on "errands", which were communications with her black market contact, [[Luthen Rael]]. At first, Karlo was evaded when he tried to trail her through town. The next day, Ferrix channels were flooded by a bulletin from the [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Pre-Mor Authority]] seeking a [[Kenari (people)|Kenari]] male resident for questioning. Having read the report, Caleen quickly closed the screen as she was interrupted by Karlo, who invited her out for a [[Foodstuff|meal]]. She promised to share it with him the following day, before exiting the salvage yard. Karlo headed over to the screen and read the notice from Pre-Mor. Having been told of Andor's origins by Caleen sometime prior, Karlo immediately recognised him as the suspect. Come nightfall, after taking a swig from his flask, Karlo approached a comm terminal to send a tip to Pre-Mor that Andor was the one they're looking for.<ref name="Episode 2">{{Andor|That Would Be Me}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Personality and traits==
Timm Karlo was a human male with medium [[Color|brown]] [[hair]], blue [[Eye|eye]]s, and light skin.<ref name="Episode 3" /> Karlo had a habit for drinking and made rash, near-sighted decisions out of jealousy and insecurity. Despite that, he cared for his girlfriend and had little concern for his own safety when he confronted armed Preox-Morlana security officers arresting her.<ref name="Episode 3" />

==Behind the scenes==
He was portrayed by [[James McArdle]].<ref name="Episode 1" />

